      "browser": "host",
      "why": "uses the standard library (`json.parse`, `json.stringify`), which the in-browser runtime does not provide",
      "expect_output": "Ada\n4\n{\"x\":1}\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-13",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Paths — `path.*`\n\n`path.join(a, b)`, `dirname`, `basename`, `extension`, `stem`, `is_absolute`,\n`normalize` — pure string manipulation, no filesystem access.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(path.join(\"a\", \"b.txt\"))\nprint(path.dirname(\"/x/y/z.txt\"))\nprint(path.basename(\"/x/y/z.txt\"))\nprint(path.stem(\"z.tar.gz\"))\nprint(path.normalize(\"a/./b/../c\"))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "needs-host"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/stdlib.md:189",
      "browser": "host",
      "why": "uses the standard library (`path.basename`, `path.dirname`, `path.join` …), which the in-browser runtime does not provide",
      "expect_output": "a/b.txt\n/x/y\nz.txt\nz.tar\na/c\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-15",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Regular expressions — `regex.*`\n\n**The pattern comes first**, then the text: `regex.test(pattern, text)`,\n`regex.find_all(pattern, text)`, `regex.replace(pattern, text, replacement)`,\n`regex.split(pattern, text)`.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-8",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(regex.find_all(\"[0-9]+\", \"a1b22\"))\nprint(regex.replace(\"[0-9]\", \"a1b2\", \"#\"))\nprint(regex.split(\"[,;] *\", \"a, b;c\"))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "needs-host"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/stdlib.md:212",
      "browser": "host",
      "why": "uses the standard library (`regex.find_all`, `regex.replace`, `regex.split`), which the in-browser runtime does not provide",
      "expect_output": "[1, 22]\na#b#\n[a, b, c]\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-17",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "> **Known bug.** `regex.match` is registered but can't be called from source:\n> `match` is a keyword, so `regex.match(...)` is a parse error (`Expected field\n> name but found match`).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-9",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(regex.match(\"([a-z]+)([0-9]+)\", \"abc123\"))\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
