  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-19",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Other families\n\nAlso registered under `--stdlib`: `bytes.*` (`from_string`, `to_string`, `len`,\n`slice`), `buffer.*` (`alloc`, `read`, `write`, `freeze`), `binary.read_*` /\n`binary.write_*` (u16/u32/u64, big/little endian), `result.*` (`ok`, `err`,\n`is_ok`, `unwrap` — results are plain `{ok, value}` objects), `text.sort`,\n`text.uniq`, `time.format`, `time.parse`, `env.os`, `env.arch`, and the `system.*`\nhelpers implemented in Crush itself (`crates/crush-lang-sdk/sbl/`).\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-10",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "print(result.unwrap(result.ok(5)))\nprint(env.os())\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "needs-host"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "crush/stdlib.md:243",
      "browser": "host",
      "why": "uses `env.os`; uses the standard library (`result.ok`, `result.unwrap`), which the in-browser runtime does not provide",
      "expect_output": "5\nlinux\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "crush-stdlib-md-21",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "(The second line depends on the machine running the example.)\n\n## Not in the library\n\nThere is no `std.*` module tree, `io.eprint`, `sys.*`, `array.length` or\n`map.*`. For output use `print`/`io.print`; for the process environment use\n`env.get` (`--env`); for arguments, there is currently no accessor.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- **[Capability System](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/capabilities.html)**\n- **[Polyglot Programming](https://docs.crushlang.org/crush/polyglot.html)**\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  }
 ]
